  "preamble": "The voiceless dental fricative [θ] becomes the sibilant [s]. Ge'ez merged Proto-Semitic *θ with s (ሰበረ säbärä 'to break' beside Arabic ṯabara), and Old Persian θ became s in Middle Persian (θarda > sāl 'year', aθaⁿga > sang 'stone').",
  "phoneticEffects": "Sibilantization",
